<Layout title="Enquiry and submission terms" description="Terms for program enquiries and non-confidential venture idea submissions to SamkhyaAcademy."><PageHero eyebrow="Terms" title="A clear starting point for a conversation." description="Terms for program enquiries and Venture Launchpad idea briefs."/><section class="container section prose narrow"><h2>What an enquiry means</h2><p>An enquiry asks the academy to discuss a program or service. It does not confirm a place, enrolment, fee, response deadline or engagement. Teaching and advisory arrangements are agreed separately.</p><h2>Your idea and your information</h2><p>You retain ownership of the material you submit. You allow the academy to review the brief and contact you about it. Do not submit another person’s confidential information or material you are not entitled to share.</p><h2>Keep the initial brief non-confidential</h2><p>Describe the problem, intended users and proposed approach without trade secrets, passwords, identity documents or private customer data. An initial submission does not establish a non-disclosure agreement. Any confidentiality agreement, implementation scope, deliverables, intellectual property arrangements and fees are agreed separately before an engagement.</p><h2>Advisory scope</h2><p>Acceptance for discussion is not a promise of funding, investment, commercial results or implementation. The academy and founder agree the scope, responsibilities and milestones for any advisory or execution work.</p><h2>Respectful and accurate submissions</h2><p>Provide contact details you are entitled to use and information that accurately describes your request. The service may limit automated, abusive or repeated submissions.</p><h2>Data handling</h2><p>Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy information</a> for the current website experience.</p><h2>Online enquiries</h2><p>Submitting a program enquiry or venture idea brief sends your details to the academy-owned Google service for review and follow-up. A confirmation reference is shown after the enquiry is saved. Contact the academy if a submission does not complete. Venture ideas use a separate brief and response workbook, with the same confirmation and consent process.</p></section></Layout>